<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; Provisional machine alignment by Codex (English-first proposal). phra ma is omitted rather than assigned GMR's distributed ‘split people up with your talk’ construction because its participant and possessive wording is not a separately alignable atom. The established terrain and travel compounds retain only source-attested English, with tighter high/low and travel/difficulty members. Explicit English order selects the first fear occurrence and places ‘many’ before the later complete fear phrase. Conjunctions, supplied scene-setting language, ‘gullies’, and the final possessive construction remain unwrapped.</div>
